From: archpower
Date: 2026-06-28
Subject: [PATCH] powerpc/dart_iommu: disable U4 DART bypass for display
 devices

The U4 CPC945 DART bypass on the PowerMac G5 x16 PCIe slot is incompatible
with r600+ (TeraScale) AMD GPUs, including Caicos (HD 6450), Cedar (HD 5450),
Turks (HD 6570), and Cayman (HD 6970). The ring buffer test (RING0) fails and
GPU acceleration gets disabled.

The bypass gives DMA addresses in the 0x8000000000+ range, and r600+ GPUs
cannot handle the resulting PCIe transactions correctly.  The same cards work
fine when:
  - Placed in the x8 slot (behind the HT bridge, through the DART IOMMU)
  - Used with DART bypass disabled via this patch (falls back to DART IOMMU)

Fix by keeping display-class devices on the IOMMU path instead of allowing
them to use the U4 DART bypass.

Signed-off-by: archpower
---
 arch/powerpc/sysdev/dart_iommu.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/powerpc/sysdev/dart_iommu.c b/arch/powerpc/sysdev/dart_iommu.c
index 2d87f9b3177e..30b457974a48 100644
--- a/arch/powerpc/sysdev/dart_iommu.c
+++ b/arch/powerpc/sysdev/dart_iommu.c
@@ -381,6 +381,13 @@ static void pci_dma_dev_setup_dart(struct pci_dev *dev)
 
 static bool iommu_bypass_supported_dart(struct pci_dev *dev, u64 mask)
 {
+	/* Display-class devices (r600+/TeraScale AMD GPUs) are known
+	 * to malfunction with the U4 DART bypass on the x16 PCIe slot.
+	 * Keep them on the IOMMU/DART path instead, which works correctly
+	 * (as proven by the same cards working in the x8 slot).
+	 */
+	if ((dev->class >> 16) == PCI_BASE_CLASS_DISPLAY)
+		return false;
 	return dart_is_u4 &&
 		dart_device_on_pcie(&dev->dev) &&
 		mask >= DMA_BIT_MASK(40);
--
2.49.0
